    {
        "id": "c1b5f18c7d4e9206",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "b82a4d69e1fa5c37",
        "name": "FIRST STEPS (double click me)",
        "x": 150,
        "y": 40,
        "wires": [],
        "info": "Click on the \"Hue Automation\" node and select both your bridge and an automation from the list. If you have not yet set up a bridge, you will be asked to set one up before you can finish configuring the node.\n\nThe automations you can select here are the ones you have created in the Philips Hue app, for example a wake up light or a coming home routine. HueMagic can enable and disable them, so you can let your flows decide when one of your routines should run at all.\n\nAs soon as the node is connected and you have deployed the changes in Node-RED, the node automatically outputs a message each time the automation changes. You will receive the updated status and all of its information in the message that is issued.\n\nIf you would like to receive more information about this node, the possible commands and output values, then click on it once in your flow and navigate to the Node-RED book icon (top right corner)."
    },
